    <solution><p><alert>A.</alert>
If <m>n = 4</m>, <m>\Delta t = \frac{8-0}{4} = 2</m>.
Thus <m>(t_0, t_1, t_2, t_3, t_4) = (0, 2, 4, 6, 8)</m> and 
<m>(f(t_0), f(t_1), f(t_2), f(t_3), f(t_4)) = (29, 25, 23, 22, 18)</m>.</p>
<p><alert>B.</alert>
The left-hand sum is</p>
<p>left sum 
<m>= 2 (29 + 25 + 23 + 22) = 198.</m></p>
<p>And the right-hand sum is</p>
<p>right sum 
<m>= 2 (25 + 23 + 22 + 18) = 176.</m></p>
<p><alert>C.</alert>
Here, <m>\Delta t = 4</m>, so 
<m>(t_0, t_1, t_2) = (0, 4, 8)</m> and
<m>(f(t_0), f(t_1), f(t_2)) = (29, 23, 18)</m>.</p>
<p><alert>D.</alert>
The left- and right-hand sums are</p>
<p>left sum <m>= 4 (29 + 23) = 208</m>, and</p>
<p>right sum <m>= 4 (23 + 18) = 164</m>, and</p>
</solution>
